From 140689fb69bff62899731bddf4313120cfd1d68c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:27:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 892/913] drivers: stm32_etzpc: remove a dead switch default
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In stm32_etzpc_configure_memory the TZMA branch is only entered when the
identifier is ETZPC_TZMA0_ID or ETZPC_TZMA1_ID, so the default case of
the switch selecting the TZMA parameters can never be reached.

Select the parameters with a simple test on the two identifiers.

Coverity issue: CID 1200827: Dead default in switch in stm32_etzpc_configure_memory

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git d616e3851f1c230da6e85e97c50675d358d3e2c8 drivers: stm32_etzpc: remove a dead switch default]
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Opus-5
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I112722b9d2de6003d0a6fafa2d5d1bc5ad774e7c
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/597013
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/firewall/stm32_etzpc.c | 9 ++-------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_etzpc.c b/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_etzpc.c
index 4112bf03a..8f7f2194a 100644
--- a/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_etzpc.c
+++ b/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_etzpc.c
@@ -581,19 +581,14 @@ static TEE_Result stm32_etzpc_configure_memory(struct firewall_query *firewall,
 		paddr_t ram_base = 0;
 		size_t ram_size = 0;
 
-		switch (id) {
-		case ETZPC_TZMA0_ID:
+		if (id == ETZPC_TZMA0_ID) {
 			ram_base = ROM_BASE;
 			ram_size = ROM_SIZE;
 			tzma_id = 0;
-			break;
-		case ETZPC_TZMA1_ID:
+		} else {
 			ram_base = SYSRAM_BASE;
 			ram_size = SYSRAM_SIZE;
 			tzma_id = 1;
-			break;
-		default:
-			return TEE_ERROR_BAD_PARAMETERS;
 		}
 
 		/* TZMA configuration supports only page aligned sizes */
-- 
